  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Utkarsh Mittal vs Food And Drugs Administration Dewas on 10 November, 2017 1 Cr.R. No.3124/2017",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "The contention of learned counsel for the petitioner is that the petitioner has been convicted for the offence under Section 7 (i) read with S.16 (i) (A) (i) and sentenced him to suffer six months rigorous imprisonment with fine of Rs.1,000/- and under Section 7(i), 7 (v), 14 (A) read with S. 16 (i) (A) (i), 16 (i) (ii), 16 (ic) of prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and sentenced him to suffer six months rigorous imprisonment with fine of Rs.1,000/- with default stipulation vide impugned judgment dated 31.03.2016 passed by the JMFC-Sonkatch- District-Dewas in Criminal Case No.581/2009 and affirmed by the Appellate Court in Criminal Appeal No.186/2016.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The contention of learned counsel for the petitioner is that the petitioner has been convicted for the offence under Section 7 (i) read with S.16 (i) (A) (i) and sentenced him to suffer six months rigorous imprisonment with fine of Rs.1,000/- and under Section 7(i), 7 (v), 14 (A) read with S. 16 (i) (A) (i), 16 (i) (ii), 16 (ic) of prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 and sentenced him to suffer six months rigorous imprisonment with fine of Rs.1,000/- with default stipulation vide impugned judgment dated 31.03.2016 passed by the JMFC-Sonkatch- District-Dewas in Criminal Case No.581/2009 and affirmed by the Appellate Court in Criminal Appeal No.186/2016.",
